\pard\sb180\sa160\b\fs31 Apple Pay Provisioning: Tokenization and Issuer Verification\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 STORAGE source: SEQUENCE_EXAMPLES.docx, Example #2, titled Apple Pay Tokenization (Visa) \u8212? Wallet-Initiated (Issuer-Assisted). The original diagram has 24 numbered interactions among cardholder, Wallet/PassKit, provisioning APIs, Visa Token Service, issuer tokenization service and secure device storage.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 This publication is a generalized learning model, not a verified or certified Apple/Visa API contract. The source includes provider-internal messages and cryptographic/key-material descriptions. The public diagram removes those implementation-specific payloads rather than asserting that they are publicly available APIs.\b0\par
\pard\sb200\sa100\b\fs25 Source participants and responsibilities\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Source actor  |  Public logical role\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Cardholder  |  Requests to add an existing card to a device\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Apple Wallet / PassKit  |  Customer-facing card provisioning UI\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Apple provisioning services  |  Manages platform-side provisioning session\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Network tokenization service (VTS in source)  |  Processes token request and token lifecycle\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Issuer token service  |  Makes eligibility/risk and step-up decisions\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Device secure storage  |  Holds authorized device payment credential\b0\par
\pard\sb200\sa100\b\fs25 Lifecycle preserved from the source\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 1. Enrollment start: cardholder selects Add Card; device capabilities and session context are checked.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 2. Card submission: Wallet sends protected provisioning information to relevant platform/network services.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 3. Issuer decision: issuer checks eligibility/risk and determines whether additional verification is required.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 4. Step-up path: SMS/call/email one-time code or redirect to issuer banking application, subject to supported methods.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 5. No-step-up path: issuer/network confirm eligibility according to applicable risk decisions.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 6. Provisioning: tokenization platform and Wallet complete secure credential activation.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 7. Completion: user sees that the card has been added; provisioning status is synchronized.\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 The original depicts tokenized PAN and wrapped key material. Their exact contract is outside this public reference. Do not treat either as plaintext business data that integrators should store.\b0\par
\pard\sb200\sa100\b\fs25 Architecture review and recovery\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Risk  |  Design review consideration\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Wallet UI reports success but token activation unfinished  |  Query authoritative token status rather than assuming active\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 OTP challenge expired or failed  |  Rate limit and use issuer-approved retry/step-up procedures\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Token created but provisioning callback lost  |  Correlate stable token/session reference; reconcile\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Device changed or removed  |  Token lifecycle suspension/deletion policies\b0\par
\pard\li180\sa75\fs18 Duplicate provisioning attempts  |  Provider-controlled enrollment correlation and dedupe\b0\par
\pard\sa100\fs19 These are new review questions, not claims of actual Visa/Apple backend behavior.\b0\par
